-- title:
--   Evaluation of the elliptic germ constant A ν_T(T_c)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, $v$ a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$ with completion $K_v$, and $c \in K_v^\times$. Let $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ satisfy: $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma_0)^2 - 4\det(\gamma_0)$ is a unit, and no conjugate $g^{-1}\gamma_0 g$ has both off-diagonal entries $0$. Write $T$ for the centraliser of $\{\gamma_0\}$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$, each such centraliser being equipped with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra, as is $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$. Let $\nu_T$ be a Borel measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ that is the pushforward under the inclusion $T \hookrightarrow \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ of some Haar measure on $T$. Let $\nu$ be a complex-valued functional on functions $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathbb{C}$, let $A \in \mathbb{C}$, and let $B : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathbb{C}$, subject to the germ hypothesis: for every locally constant, compactly supported $f : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathbb{C}$ there is a neighbourhood $W$ of the scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ such that for all $\gamma \in W \cap T$ with $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2 - 4\det(\gamma)$ a unit, every Haar measure $\tau$ on the centraliser of $\{\gamma\}$ pushing forward to $\nu_T$, and every $I \in \mathbb{C}$ representable as $I = \int f(x^{-1}\gamma x)\, w(x)\, dx$ against the fixed Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ for some nonnegative measurable compactly supported $w$ with $\int_{Z(\gamma)} w(tx)\, d\tau(t) = 1$ whenever $f(x^{-1}\gamma x) \neq 0$, one has $I = A\, f(c \cdot 1) + B(\gamma)\,\nu(f)$. Then, setting $T_c = \{g \in T : v(\det g) = 1,\ v(\mathrm{tr}\, g) \le 1\}$ and $q = \mathrm{absNorm}(v)$: if some $t \in T$ has $v(\det t) = \mathrm{ofAdd}(-1)$ then $A \cdot \nu_T(T_c) = -1/(q-1)$, and if no such $t$ exists then $A \cdot \nu_T(T_c) = -2/(q-1)$, the real measure value being coerced into $\mathbb{C}$.
--
--   This is the computation of the constant attached to the point $c \cdot 1$ in the germ expansion of elliptic orbital integrals on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$: its value is $-f(E/K_v)/(q_v-1)$, where $E = K_v(\gamma_0)$ is the quadratic field generated by the elliptic element and the ramification of $E/K_v$ is detected here by whether the determinant valuation on the centraliser attains an odd value. The statement is formulated for an arbitrary germ datum $(\nu, A, B)$, so that it reads off $A$ without identifying the unipotent functional $\nu$; it is used in the comparison of twisted and ordinary orbital integrals that feeds the base-change argument.
